[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Create the bounded developer-documentation closure for the SHARD-01 foundation.
[stderr] +It cross-references the approved planning contracts for architecture ownership,
[stderr] +command flow, save-versus-cache recovery, and P0 connected-scope exclusion.
[stderr] +It is documentation work only: it neither implements these boundaries nor
[stderr] +claims their approval, product completion, or release readiness.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0002 defines the shared-core and adapter seam; R0004 owns deterministic
[stderr] +campaign-state transitions; R0006 owns the local save and recovery protocol;
[stderr] +and R0008 owns the P0 identity and connected-service exclusion. Their listed
[stderr] +contracts are prerequisites for this index, not evidence that implementation
[stderr] +or the B0004 checkpoint has been accepted. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 for
[stderr] +storage, quota, support, and recovery-policy choices, and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006
[stderr] +for any connected scope. No documented gate is resolved here.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `docs/architecture.md` foundation component, dependency-direction, and
[stderr] +  public-boundary inventory.
[stderr] +- `docs/development.md` command-flow, validation, and ownership cross-reference.
[stderr] +- `docs/save-and-recovery.md` save-versus-preference-versus-cache boundary and
[stderr] +  recovery index.
[stderr] +- `docs/security-boundary.md` P0 local-profile and connected-scope exclusion.
[stderr] +- Foundation decision and ownership index, and the documented public-boundary
[stderr] +  inventory.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +This contract owns the required documentation set and its cross-reference
[stderr] +index only. R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008 retain ownership of their seams,
[stderr] +state, persistence protocol, negative boundary tests, and any implementation
[stderr] +outputs. Content validation, migration execution, PWA release/cache lifecycle,
[stderr] +diagnostics, assets, and audio remain with their respective current or future
[stderr] +contracts.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Document the foundation architecture as a shared deterministic rules core,
[stderr] +content validator, browser presentation/input adapters, local save/recovery
[stderr] +repository, PWA release manager, and error/diagnostic boundary. State the
[stderr] +direction of interaction: adapters issue commands, only the rules core produces
[stderr] +durable campaign state, and the shell renders returned state/events without
[stderr] +mutating campaign state. Browser APIs, timers, network calls, and renderer
[stderr] +dependencies remain outside the core.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Document that the save repository owns serialized snapshots and recovery
[stderr] +metadata, while the shell owns ephemeral UI state. Record the write-ahead
[stderr] +replacement boundary: validate a complete candidate and read-back before
[stderr] +promoting a current pointer, retain a known-good snapshot, and quarantine
[stderr] +invalid or incompatible candidates. Preferences and PWA cache records are not
[stderr] +saves and cannot promote, overwrite, delete, synchronise, or imply success for
[stderr] +a campaign snapshot. Migration transformations remain a later pure-runner
[stderr] +concern; this index must not choose storage, quota, retention, support window,
[stderr] +or migration policy.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Document P0 as an offline local-profile boundary with no account, token, role,
[stderr] +remote profile, network client, cloud save, analytics transport, entitlement,
[stderr] +or connected campaign authority. Treat persisted bytes, content, browser
[stderr] +events, URL parameters, and service-worker messages as untrusted at their
[stderr] +respective boundaries. Any future connected proposal remains separately gated
[stderr] +and cannot redefine the local campaign as non-authoritative.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Responsive web and installed PWA share the same core, command, local-save,
[stderr] +preference, quarantine, and connected-scope boundaries. The PWA release/cache
[stderr] +manager may manage install and cached-release lifecycle but must remain separate
[stderr] +from campaign persistence: a cache refresh, update, or offline failure cannot
[stderr] +alter a confirmed save. This documentation does not select a browser-storage
[stderr] +mechanism, service-worker rollout policy, browser matrix, or PWA implementation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not implement or approve a framework, renderer, storage API, quota,
[stderr] +retention or support policy, migration set, diagnostics vendor or transport,
[stderr] +identity, authorization, remote service, cloud sync, telemetry, purchase,
[stderr] +entitlement, rollout, release operation, or player-facing release guide. Do
[stderr] +not claim vendor, security, privacy, legal, product, or release approval. Do
[stderr] +not create gameplay, UI, content, assets, audio, source implementation, or
[stderr] +test fixtures beyond the documentation contract described above.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: foundation documentation and its ownership
[stderr] +index need no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental visual, source,
[stderr] +audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other product asset;
[stderr] +`asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.
[stderr] +
