3\\nasset_impact: not_applicable\\nasset_ids:\\naudio_impact: not_applicable\\naudio_ids:\\naudio_brief:\\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\\naudio_loop: not_applicable\\naudio_style_version:\\n---\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\nDo the work.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- The work is done.\\n\",\nsupervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py:106:        \"---\\ntask_id: R0002\\nsequence: 2\\ntitle: Invalid dependency\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec:\\ndependencies: R0001,not-a-task\\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#loop\\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-LOOP-002\\nauthoring_batch: B0001\\nfactory_stages: F002,F012,F013\\nasset_impact: not_applicable\\nasset_ids:\\naudio_impact: not_applicable\\naudio_ids:\\naudio_brief:\\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\\naudio_loop: not_applicable\\naudio_style_version:\\n---\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\nDo the work.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- The work is done.\\n\",\n\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..682eca0b41aab322e6bfcecdbe577a6f46d2f32f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,152 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0012\n+sequence: 12\n+title: Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\n+dependencies: R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008\n+requirement_ids: NFR-0012,NFR-0010,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability,specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0012\n+authoring_batch: B0006\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create the bounded developer-documentation closure for the SHARD-01 foundation.\n+It cross-references the approved planning contracts for architecture ownership,\n+command flow, save-versus-cache recovery, and P0 connected-scope exclusion.\n+It is documentation work only: it neither implements these boundaries nor\n+claims their approval, product completion, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 defines the shared-core and adapter seam; R0004 owns deterministic\n+campaign-state transitions; R0006 owns the local save and recovery protocol;\n+and R0008 owns the P0 identity and connected-service exclusion. Their listed\n+contracts are prerequisites for this index, not evidence that implementation\n+or the B0004 checkpoint has been accepted. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 for\n+storage, quota, support, and recovery-policy choices, and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\n+for any connected scope. No documented gate is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/architecture.md` foundation component, dependency-direction, and\n+  public-boundary inventory.\n+- `docs/development.md` command-flow, validation, and ownership cross-reference.\n+- `docs/save-and-recovery.md` save-versus-preference-versus-cache boundary and\n+  recovery index.\n+- `docs/security-boundary.md` P0 local-profile and connected-scope exclusion.\n+- Foundation decision and ownership index, and the documented public-boundary\n+  inventory.\n+\n+This contract owns the required documentation set and its cross-reference\n+index only. R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008 retain ownership of their seams,\n+state, persistence protocol, negative boundary tests, and any implementation\n+outputs. Content validation, migration execution, PWA release/cache lifecycle,\n+diagnostics, assets, and audio remain with their respective current or future\n+contracts.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Document the foundation architecture as a shared deterministic rules core,\n+content validator, browser presentation/input adapters, local save/recovery\n+repository, PWA release manager, and error/diagnostic boundary. State the\n+direction of interaction: adapters issue commands, only the rules core produces\n+durable campaign state, and the shell renders returned state/events without\n+mutating campaign state. Browser APIs, timers, network calls, and renderer\n+dependencies remain outside the core.\n+\n+Document that the save repository owns serialized snapshots and recovery\n+metadata, while the shell owns ephemeral UI state. Record the write-ahead\n+replacement boundary: validate a complete candidate and read-back before\n+promoting a current pointer, retain a known-good snapshot, and quarantine\n+invalid or incompatible candidates. Preferences and PWA cache records are not\n+saves and cannot promote, overwrite, delete, synchronise, or imply success for\n+a campaign snapshot. Migration transformations remain a later pure-runner\n+concern; this index must not choose storage, quota, retention, support window,\n+or migration policy.\n+\n+Document P0 as an offline local-profile boundary with no account, token, role,\n+remote profile, network client, cloud save, analytics transport, entitlement,\n+or connected campaign authority. Treat persisted bytes, content, browser\n+events, URL parameters, and service-worker messages as untrusted at their\n+respective boundaries. Any future connected proposal remains separately gated\n+and cannot redefine the local campaign as non-authoritative.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA share the same core, command, local-save,\n+preference, quarantine, and connected-scope boundaries. The PWA release/cache\n+manager may manage install and cached-release lifecycle but must remain separate\n+from campaign persistence: a cache refresh, update, or offline failure cannot\n+alter a confirmed save. This documentation does not select a browser-storage\n+mechanism, service-worker rollout policy, browser matrix, or PWA implementation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement or approve a framework, renderer, storage API, quota,\n+retention or support policy, migration set, diagnostics vendor or transport,\n+identity, authorization, remote service, cloud sync, telemetry, purchase,\n+entitlement, rollout, release operation, or player-facing release guide. Do\n+not claim vendor, security, privacy, legal, product, or release approval. Do\n+not create gameplay, UI, content, assets, audio, source implementation, or\n+test fixtures beyond the documentation contract described above.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: foundation documentation and its ownership\n+index need no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental visual, source,\n+audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other product asset;\n+`asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Load this runbook and compare its task ID, sequence, title, catalogue ID,\n+  requirement IDs, source specifications, dependencies, authoring batch,\n+  factory stages, and asset/audio/browser decisions with the R0012 manifest\n+  allocation and IMP-0012 catalogue record.\n+- Cross-check the documentation index against R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008:\n+  each prerequisite's ownership, dependency boundary, and retained gate must\n+  be named without transferring ownership or claiming implementation status.\n+- Confirm the index distinguishes durable campaign state, serialized snapshot\n+  and recovery metadata, preferences, PWA cache, shell UI state, and future\n+  connected scope; confirm it contains no storage/vendor/policy selection.\n+- Confirm the documentation records GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 /\n+  DEC-0006 as unresolved. If R0006 or B0004 is blocked, preserve that state in\n+  the cross-check; do not mark the foundation, a gate, or a release accepted.\n+- Record the B0006 checkpoint only after every comparison succeeds. On a\n+  mismatch or existing conflicting R0012 contract, stop, retain the allocated\n+  ID and path, and repair or report only this documentation contract; never\n+  overwrite, reuse, renumber, or replace an R ID.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the loader result; manifest and IMP-0012 comparison record; the\n+foundation ownership/dependency/gate matrix for R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008;\n+the save/preference/cache and local/connected-boundary review; all retained\n+GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 records; and the successful\n+pre-checkpoint validation record. These are contract-review artefacts, not\n+evidence of implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The developer-documentation closure maps every listed foundation prerequisite\n+  to its retained ownership, dependency boundary, and unresolved gate without\n+  transferring implementation ownership or claiming acceptance.\n+- Architecture, command flow, save/recovery, preference/cache separation, and\n+  P0 connected-scope exclusion remain explicit for both responsive web and PWA\n+  delivery paths.\n+- No product asset, implementation, approval, vendor/policy choice, or release\n+  readiness claim is introduced; GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\n+  remain visible.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..682eca0b41aab322e6bfcecdbe577a6f46d2f32f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,152 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0012\n+sequence: 12\n+title: Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\n+dependencies: R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008\n+requirement_ids: NFR-0012,NFR-0010,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability,specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0012\n+authoring_batch: B0006\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create the bounded developer-documentation closure for the SHARD-01 foundation.\n+It cross-references the approved planning contracts for architecture ownership,\n+command flow, save-versus-cache recovery, and P0 connected-scope exclusion.\n+It is documentation work only: it neither implements these boundaries nor\n+claims their approval, product completion, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 defines the shared-core and adapter seam; R0004 owns deterministic\n+campaign-state transitions; R0006 owns the local save and recovery protocol;\n+and R0008 owns the P0 identity and connected-service exclusion. Their listed\n+contracts are prerequisites for this index, not evidence that implementation\n+or the B0004 checkpoint has been accepted. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 for\n+storage, quota, support, and recovery-policy choices, and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\n+for any connected scope. No documented gate is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/architecture.md` foundation component, dependency-direction, and\n+  public-boundary inventory.\n+- `docs/development.md` command-flow, validation, and ownership cross-reference.\n+- `docs/save-and-recovery.md` save-versus-preference-versus-cache boundary and\n+  recovery index.\n+- `docs/security-boundary.md` P0 local-profile and connected-scope exclusion.\n+- Foundation decision and ownership index, and the documented public-boundary\n+  inventory.\n+\n+This contract owns the required documentation set and its cross-reference\n+index only. R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008 retain ownership of their seams,\n+state, persistence protocol, negative boundary tests, and any implementation\n+outputs. Content validation, migration execution, PWA release/cache lifecycle,\n+diagnostics, assets, and audio remain with their respective current or future\n+contracts.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Document the foundation architecture as a shared deterministic rules core,\n+content validator, browser presentation/input adapters, local save/recovery\n+repository, PWA release manager, and error/diagnostic boundary. State the\n+direction of interaction: adapters issue commands, only the rules core produces\n+durable campaign state, and the shell renders returned state/events without\n+mutating campaign state. Browser APIs, timers, network calls, and renderer\n+dependencies remain outside the core.\n+\n+Document that the save repository owns serialized snapshots and recovery\n+metadata, while the shell owns ephemeral UI state. Record the write-ahead\n+replacement boundary: validate a complete candidate and read-back before\n+promoting a current pointer, retain a known-good snapshot, and quarantine\n+invalid or incompatible candidates. Preferences and PWA cache records are not\n+saves and cannot promote, overwrite, delete, synchronise, or imply success for\n+a campaign snapshot. Migration transformations remain a later pure-runner\n+concern; this index must not choose storage, quota, retention, support window,\n+or migration policy.\n+\n+Document P0 as an offline local-profile boundary with no account, token, role,\n+remote profile, network client, cloud save, analytics transport, entitlement,\n+or connected campaign authority. Treat persisted bytes, content, browser\n+events, URL parameters, and service-worker messages as untrusted at their\n+respective boundaries. Any future connected proposal remains separately gated\n+and cannot redefine the local campaign as non-authoritative.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA share the same core, command, local-save,\n+preference, quarantine, and connected-scope boundaries. The PWA release/cache\n+manager may manage install and cached-release lifecycle but must remain separate\n+from campaign persistence: a cache refresh, update, or offline failure cannot\n+alter a confirmed save. This documentation does not select a browser-storage\n+mechanism, service-worker rollout policy, browser matrix, or PWA implementation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement or approve a framework, renderer, storage API, quota,\n+retention or support policy, migration set, diagnostics vendor or transport,\n+identity, authorization, remote service, cloud sync, telemetry, purchase,\n+entitlement, rollout, release operation, or player-facing release guide. Do\n+not claim vendor, security, privacy, legal, product, or release approval. Do\n+not create gameplay, UI, content, assets, audio, source implementation, or\n+test fixtures beyond the documentation contract described above.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: foundation documentation and its ownership\n+index need no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental visual, source,\n+audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other product asset;\n+`asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Load this runbook and compare its task ID, sequence, title, catalogue ID,\n+  requirement IDs, source specifications, dependencies, authoring batch,\n+  factory stages, and asset/audio/browser decisions with the R0012 manifest\n+  allocation and IMP-0012 catalogue record.\n+- Cross-check the documentation index against R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008:\n+  each prerequisite's ownership, dependency boundary, and retained gate must\n+  be named without transferring ownership or claiming implementation status.\n+- Confirm the index distinguishes durable campaign state, serialized snapshot\n+  and recovery metadata, preferences, PWA cache, shell UI state, and future\n+  connected scope; confirm it contains no storage/vendor/policy selection.\n+- Confirm the documentation records GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 /\n+  DEC-0006 as unresolved. If R0006 or B0004 is blocked, preserve that state in\n+  the cross-check; do not mark the foundation, a gate, or a release accepted.\n+- Record the B0006 checkpoint only after every comparison succeeds. On a\n+  mismatch or existing conflicting R0012 contract, stop, retain the allocated\n+  ID and path, and repair or report only this documentation contract; never\n+  overwrite, reuse, renumber, or replace an R ID.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the loader result; manifest and IMP-0012 comparison record; the\n+foundation ownership/dependency/gate matrix for R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008;\n+the save/preference/cache and local/connected-boundary review; all retained\n+GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 records; and the successful\n+pre-checkpoint validation record. These are contract-review artefacts, not\n+evidence of implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The developer-documentation closure maps every listed foundation prerequisite\n+  to its retained ownership, dependency boundary, and unresolved gate without\n+  transferring implementation ownership or claiming acceptance.\n+- Architecture, command flow, save/recovery, preference/cache separation, and\n+  P0 connected-scope exclusion remain explicit for both responsive web and PWA\n+  delivery paths.\n+- No product asset, implementation, approval, vendor/policy choice, or release\n+  readiness claim is introduced; GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\n+  remain visible.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,155p' supervisor/supervisor/runbooks.py; sed -n '1,135p' supervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n\"\"\"Load one scoped Markdown runbook into the supervisor task contract.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom .models import Task\n\n\ndef _section(document: str, heading: str) -> str:\n    match = re.search(rf\"^## {re.escape(heading)}\\s*$\\n(.*?)(?=^## |\\Z)\", document, re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)\n    if not match:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Runbook is missing a ## {heading} section.\")\n    return match.group(1).strip()\n\n\ndef load_task(path: Path) -> Task:\n    \"\"\"Parse the deliberately small runbook format and its execution gates.\"\"\"\n\n    document = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    metadata_match = re.match(r\"^---\\n(.*?)\\n---\\n\", document, re.DOTALL)\n    if not metadata_match:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{path} must start with YAML-style metadata.\")\n    metadata: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for line in metadata_match.group(1).splitlines():\n        key, separator, value = line.partition(\":\")\n        if not separator:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid runbook metadata line: {line}\")\n        metadata[key.strip()] = value.strip()\n    required = {\"task_id\", \"sequence\", \"title\", \"browser_impact\", \"playwright_spec\"}\n    missing = required - metadata.keys()\n    if missing:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{path} is missing metadata: {', '.join(sorted(missing))}\")\n    is_r_series = re.fullmatch(r\"R\\d+\", metadata[\"task_id\"]) is not None\n    if is_r_series:\n        dependencies = [value.strip() for value in metadata.get(\"dependencies\", \"\").split(\",\") if value.strip()]\n        if len(dependencies) != len(set(dependencies)) or any(not re.fullmatch(r\"R\\d+\", dependency) for dependency in dependencies):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} has invalid dependencies; use comma-separated R-series IDs.\")\n        if metadata[\"task_id\"] in dependencies:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} cannot depend on itself.\")\n        provenance_metadata = {\"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\"}\n        missing_provenance_metadata = provenance_metadata - metadata.keys()\n        if missing_provenance_metadata:\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"{path} is an R-series runbook and must declare provenance metadata: \"\n                f\"{', '.join(sorted(missing_provenance_metadata))}\"\n            )\n        source_specifications = [value.strip() for value in metadata[\"source_specifications\"].split(\",\") if value.strip()]\n        source_catalogue_ids = [value.strip() for value in metadata[\"source_catalogue_ids\"].split(\",\") if value.strip()]\n        factory_stages = [value.strip() for value in metadata[\"factory_stages\"].split(\",\") if value.strip()]\n        if not source_specifications or not source_catalogue_ids or not factory_stages:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} has incomplete R-series provenance metadata.\")\n        if not re.fullmatch(r\"B\\d+\", metadata[\"authoring_batch\"]):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} has invalid authoring_batch; use an ID such as B0001.\")\n        if any(not re.fullmatch(r\"F\\d+\", stage) for stage in factory_stages):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} has invalid factory_stages; use comma-separated F-series IDs.\")\n        asset_metadata = {\"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"}\n        missing_asset_metadata = asset_metadata - metadata.keys()\n        if missing_asset_metadata:\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"{path} is an R-series runbook and must declare asset metadata: \"\n                f\"{', '.join(sorted(missing_asset_metadata))}\"\n            )\n        if metadata[\"asset_impact\"] not in {\"required\", \"not_applicable\"}:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} has invalid asset_impact; use required or not_applicable.\")\n        declared_assets = [asset_id.strip() for asset_id in metadata[\"asset_ids\"].split(\",\") if asset_id.strip()]\n        if metadata[\"asset_impact\"] == \"required\" and not declared_assets:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} requires assets but has no asset_ids.\")\n        if metadata[\"asset_impact\"] == \"not_applicable\" and declared_assets:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} declares asset_ids but asset_impact is not_applicable.\")\n        audio_metadata = {\"audio_impact\", \"audio_ids\", \"audio_brief\", \"audio_duration_seconds\", \"audio_loop\", \"audio_style_version\"}\n        missing_audio_metadata = audio_metadata - metadata.keys()\n        if missing_audio_metadata:\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"{path} is an R-series runbook and must declare audio metadata: \"\n                f\"{', '.join(sorted(missing_audio_metadata))}\"\n            )\n        if metadata[\"audio_impact\"] not in {\"required\", \"not_applicable\"}:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} has invalid audio_impact; use required or not_applicable.\")\n        declared_audio = [audio_id.strip() for audio_id in metadata[\"audio_ids\"].split(\",\") if audio_id.strip()]\n        if metadata[\"audio_impact\"] == \"required\":\n            if not declared_audio or not metadata[\"audio_brief\"].strip():\n                raise ValueError(f\"{path} requires audio but has no audio_ids or audio_brief.\")\n            try:\n                duration = int(metadata[\"audio_duration_seconds\"])\n            except ValueError as error:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{path} has invalid audio_duration_seconds.\") from error\n            if duration < 1:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{path} requires audio_duration_seconds greater than zero.\")\n            if metadata[\"audio_loop\"] not in {\"required\", \"not_required\"}:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{path} has invalid audio_loop; use required or not_required.\")\n        elif declared_audio or metadata[\"audio_brief\"].strip() or metadata[\"audio_duration_seconds\"].strip() not in {\"\", \"0\"} or metadata[\"audio_loop\"] not in {\"\", \"not_applicable\"}:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path} declares audio fields but audio_impact is not_applicable.\")\n    criteria: list[str] = []\n    current: list[str] = []\n    for line in _section(document, \"Acceptance criteria\").splitlines():\n        if line.startswith(\"- \"):\n            if current:\n                criteria.append(\" \".join(current))\n            current = [line[2:].strip()]\n        elif current and line.strip():\n            # Markdown permits a hanging indent for a long bullet. Preserve\n            # the entire criterion so it remains a precise worker contract.\n            current.append(line.strip())\n    if current:\n        criteria.append(\" \".join(current))\n    if not criteria:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{path} has no acceptance criteria.\")\n    return Task(\n        task_id=metadata[\"task_id\"],\n        title=metadata[\"title\"],\n        sequence=int(metadata[\"sequence\"]),\n        dependencies=[value.strip() for value in metadata.get(\"dependencies\", \"\").split(\",\") if value.strip()],\n        browser_impact=metadata[\"browser_impact\"],\n        playwright_specs=[metadata[\"playwright_spec\"]] if metadata[\"playwright_spec\"] else [],\n        objective=_section(document, \"Objective\"),\n        acceptance_criteria=criteria,\n        asset_impact=metadata.get(\"asset_impact\", \"not_applicable\"),\n        asset_brief=metadata.get(\"asset_brief\", \"\"),\n        asset_ids=[asset_id.strip() for asset_id in metadata.get(\"asset_ids\", \"\").split(\",\") if asset_id.strip()],\n        visual_style_version=metadata.get(\"visual_style_version\", \"\"),\n        audio_impact=metadata.get(\"audio_impact\", \"not_applicable\"),\n        audio_brief=metadata.get(\"audio_brief\", \"\"),\n        audio_ids=[audio_id.strip() for audio_id in metadata.get(\"audio_ids\", \"\").split(\",\") if audio_id.strip()],\n        audio_duration_seconds=int(metadata.get(\"audio_duration_seconds\", \"0\") or 0),\n        audio_loop=metadata.get(\"audio_loop\", \"not_applicable\"),\n        audio_style_version=metadata.get(\"audio_style_version\", \"\"),\n        source_specifications=[value.strip() for value in metadata.get(\"source_specifications\", \"\").split(\",\") if value.strip()],\n        source_catalogue_ids=[value.strip() for value in metadata.get(\"source_catalogue_ids\", \"\").split(\",\") if value.strip()],\n        authoring_batch=metadata.get(\"authoring_batch\", \"\"),\n        factory_stages=[value.strip() for value in metadata.get(\"factory_stages\", \"\").split(\",\") if value.strip()],\n    )\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom supervisor.runbooks import load_task\n\n\ndef test_d005_runbook_loads_the_persistence_contract():\n    root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n    task = load_task(root / \"runbooks\" / \"D005.md\")\n    assert task.task_id == \"D005\"\n    assert task.sequence == 5\n    assert \"persistence\" in task.objective.lower()\n    assert task.playwright_specs == [\"tests/changes/d005-settings-restore.spec.cjs\"]\n    assert len(task.acceptance_criteria) == 8\n\n\ndef test_every_installed_runbook_loads_and_matches_its_filename():\n    root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n    for path in (root / \"runbooks\").glob(\"D*.md\"):\n        task = load_task(path)\n        assert task.task_id == path.stem\n        if task.browser_impact == \"required\":\n            assert task.playwright_specs\n        else:\n            assert not task.playwright_specs\n\n\ndef test_wrapped_acceptance_bullets_are_loaded_in_full():\n    root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n    task = load_task(root / \"runbooks\" / \"D011.md\")\n\n    assert task.acceptance_criteria[0].endswith(\n        \"raw presentation colour literals are introduced outside palette/theme code.\"\n    )\n    assert task.acceptance_criteria[-1] == (\n        \"Only this semantic-colour slice, its tests, and its browser evidence are committed.\"\n    )\n\n\ndef test_runbook_accepts_opt_in_asset_metadata(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"R0002.md\"\n    path.write_text(\n        \"---\\ntask_id: R0002\\nsequence: 1\\ntitle: Gate\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec: \\n\"\n            \"asset_impact: required\\nasset_brief: docs/art/briefs/gate.md\\nasset_ids: gate,gate_build\\nvisual_style_version: project-v1\\naudio_impact: not_applicable\\naudio_ids: \\naudio_brief: \\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\\naudio_loop: not_applicable\\naudio_style_version: \\nsource_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#gate\\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-WORLD-001\\nauthoring_batch: B0001\\nfactory_stages: F004,F012,F013\\n---\\n\"\n        \"# R0002\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\nMake a gate.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- It is original.\\n\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    )\n    task = load_task(path)\n    assert task.asset_impact == \"required\"\n    assert task.asset_ids == [\"gate\", \"gate_build\"]\n    assert task.authoring_batch == \"B0001\"\n    assert task.source_catalogue_ids == [\"IMP-WORLD-001\"]\n    assert task.visual_style_version == \"project-v1\"\n\n\ndef test_r_series_runbook_must_explicitly_assess_assets(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"R0001.md\"\n    path.write_text(\n        \"---\\ntask_id: R0001\\nsequence: 1\\ntitle: Missing asset assessment\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec:\\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#loop\\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-LOOP-001\\nauthoring_batch: B0001\\nfactory_stages: F002,F012,F013\\n---\\n\"\n        \"## Objective\\n\\nDo the work.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- The work is done.\\n\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    )\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"must declare asset metadata\"):\n        load_task(path)\n\n\ndef test_r_series_runbook_must_declare_provenance(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"R0001.md\"\n    path.write_text(\n        \"---\\ntask_id: R0001\\nsequence: 1\\ntitle: Missing provenance\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec:\\nasset_impact: not_applicable\\nasset_ids:\\n---\\n\"\n        \"## Objective\\n\\nDo the work.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- The work is done.\\n\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    )\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"must declare provenance metadata\"):\n        load_task(path)\n\n\ndef test_r_series_asset_task_requires_stable_asset_ids(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"R0001.md\"\n    path.write_text(\n        \"---\\ntask_id: R0001\\nsequence: 1\\ntitle: Asset work\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec:\\nasset_impact: required\\nasset_ids:\\nsource_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#gate\\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-WORLD-001\\nauthoring_batch: B0001\\nfactory_stages: F004,F012,F013\\n---\\n\"\n        \"## Objective\\n\\nDo the work.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- The work is done.\\n\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    )\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"has no asset_ids\"):\n        load_task(path)\n\n\ndef test_r_series_dependencies_are_loaded_as_execution_gates(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"R0002.md\"\n    path.write_text(\n        \"---\\ntask_id: R0002\\nsequence: 2\\ntitle: Dependency task\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec:\\ndependencies: R0001,R0003\\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#loop\\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-LOOP-002\\nauthoring_batch: B0001\\nfactory_stages: F002,F012,F013\\nasset_impact: not_applicable\\nasset_ids:\\naudio_impact: not_applicable\\naudio_ids:\\naudio_brief:\\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\\naudio_loop: not_applicable\\naudio_style_version:\\n---\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\nDo the work.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- The work is done.\\n\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    )\n\n    assert load_task(path).dependencies == [\"R0001\", \"R0003\"]\n\n\ndef test_r_series_dependencies_reject_invalid_ids(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"R0002.md\"\n    path.write_text(\n        \"---\\ntask_id: R0002\\nsequence: 2\\ntitle: Invalid dependency\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec:\\ndependencies: R0001,not-a-task\\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#loop\\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-LOOP-002\\nauthoring_batch: B0001\\nfactory_stages: F002,F012,F013\\nasset_impact: not_applicable\\nasset_ids:\\naudio_impact: not_applicable\\naudio_ids:\\naudio_brief:\\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\\naudio_loop: not_applicable\\naudio_style_version:\\n---\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\nDo the work.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- The work is done.\\n\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    )\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"invalid dependencies\"):\n        load_task(path)\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..682eca0b41aab322e6bfcecdbe577a6f46d2f32f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,152 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0012\n+sequence: 12\n+title: Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\n+dependencies: R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008\n+requirement_ids: NFR-0012,NFR-0010,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability,specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0012\n+authoring_batch: B0006\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Create the bounded developer-documentation closure for the SHARD-01 foundation.\n+It cross-references the approved planning contracts for architecture ownership,\n+command flow, save-versus-cache recovery, and P0 connected-scope exclusion.\n+It is documentation work only: it neither implements these boundaries nor\n+claims their approval, product completion, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 defines the shared-core and adapter seam; R0004 owns deterministic\n+campaign-state transitions; R0006 owns the local save and recovery protocol;\n+and R0008 owns the P0 identity and connected-service exclusion. Their listed\n+contracts are prerequisites for this index, not evidence that implementation\n+or the B0004 checkpoint has been accepted. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 for\n+storage, quota, support, and recovery-policy choices, and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\n+for any connected scope. No documented gate is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/architecture.md` foundation component, dependency-direction, and\n+  public-boundary inventory.\n+- `docs/development.md` command-flow, validation, and ownership cross-reference.\n+- `docs/save-and-recovery.md` save-versus-preference-versus-cache boundary and\n+  recovery index.\n+- `docs/security-boundary.md` P0 local-profile and connected-scope exclusion.\n+- Foundation decision and ownership index, and the documented public-boundary\n+  inventory.\n+\n+This contract owns the required documentation set and its cross-reference\n+index only. R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008 retain ownership of their seams,\n+state, persistence protocol, negative boundary tests, and any implementation\n+outputs. Content validation, migration execution, PWA release/cache lifecycle,\n+diagnostics, assets, and audio remain with their respective current or future\n+contracts.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Document the foundation architecture as a shared deterministic rules core,\n+content validator, browser presentation/input adapters, local save/recovery\n+repository, PWA release manager, and error/diagnostic boundary. State the\n+direction of interaction: adapters issue commands, only the rules core produces\n+durable campaign state, and the shell renders returned state/events without\n+mutating campaign state. Browser APIs, timers, network calls, and renderer\n+dependencies remain outside the core.\n+\n+Document that the save repository owns serialized snapshots and recovery\n+metadata, while the shell owns ephemeral UI state. Record the write-ahead\n+replacement boundary: validate a complete candidate and read-back before\n+promoting a current pointer, retain a known-good snapshot, and quarantine\n+invalid or incompatible candidates. Preferences and PWA cache records are not\n+saves and cannot promote, overwrite, delete, synchronise, or imply success for\n+a campaign snapshot. Migration transformations remain a later pure-runner\n+concern; this index must not choose storage, quota, retention, support window,\n+or migration policy.\n+\n+Document P0 as an offline local-profile boundary with no account, token, role,\n+remote profile, network client, cloud save, analytics transport, entitlement,\n+or connected campaign authority. Treat persisted bytes, content, browser\n+events, URL parameters, and service-worker messages as untrusted at their\n+respective boundaries. Any future connected proposal remains separately gated\n+and cannot redefine the local campaign as non-authoritative.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA share the same core, command, local-save,\n+preference, quarantine, and connected-scope boundaries. The PWA release/cache\n+manager may manage install and cached-release lifecycle but must remain separate\n+from campaign persistence: a cache refresh, update, or offline failure cannot\n+alter a confirmed save. This documentation does not select a browser-storage\n+mechanism, service-worker rollout policy, browser matrix, or PWA implementation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement or approve a framework, renderer, storage API, quota,\n+retention or support policy, migration set, diagnostics vendor or transport,\n+identity, authorization, remote service, cloud sync, telemetry, purchase,\n+entitlement, rollout, release operation, or player-facing release guide. Do\n+not claim vendor, security, privacy, legal, product, or release approval. Do\n+not create gameplay, UI, content, assets, audio, source implementation, or\n+test fixtures beyond the documentation contract described above.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: foundation documentation and its ownership\n+index need no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental visual, source,\n+audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other product asset;\n+`asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Load this runbook and compare its task ID, sequence, title, catalogue ID,\n+  requirement IDs, source specifications, dependencies, authoring batch,\n+  factory stages, and asset/audio/browser decisions with the R0012 manifest\n+  allocation and IMP-0012 catalogue record.\n+- Cross-check the documentation index against R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008:\n+  each prerequisite's ownership, dependency boundary, and retained gate must\n+  be named without transferring ownership or claiming implementation status.\n+- Confirm the index distinguishes durable campaign state, serialized snapshot\n+  and recovery metadata, preferences, PWA cache, shell UI state, and future\n+  connected scope; confirm it contains no storage/vendor/policy selection.\n+- Confirm the documentation records GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 /\n+  DEC-0006 as unresolved. If R0006 or B0004 is blocked, preserve that state in\n+  the cross-check; do not mark the foundation, a gate, or a release accepted.\n+- Record the B0006 checkpoint only after every comparison succeeds. On a\n+  mismatch or existing conflicting R0012 contract, stop, retain the allocated\n+  ID and path, and repair or report only this documentation contract; never\n+  overwrite, reuse, renumber, or replace an R ID.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the loader result; manifest and IMP-0012 comparison record; the\n+foundation ownership/dependency/gate matrix for R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008;\n+the save/preference/cache and local/connected-boundary review; all retained\n+GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 records; and the successful\n+pre-checkpoint validation record. These are contract-review artefacts, not\n+evidence of implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The developer-documentation closure maps every listed foundation prerequisite\n+  to its retained ownership, dependency boundary, and unresolved gate without\n+  transferring implementation ownership or claiming acceptance.\n+- Architecture, command flow, save/recovery, preference/cache separation, and\n+  P0 connected-scope exclusion remain explicit for both responsive web and PWA\n+  delivery paths.\n+- No product asset, implementation, approval, vendor/policy choice, or release\n+  readiness claim is introduced; GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\n+  remain visible.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=supervisor python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; from supervisor.runbooks import load_task; root=Path(\\\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4\\\"); task=load_task(root/\\\"runbooks/R0012.md\\\"); manifest=json.loads((root/\\\"planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\\\").read_text()); record=next(item for item in manifest[\\\"r_contracts\\\"] if item[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"R0012\\\"); assert task.task_id==\\\"R0012\\\"; assert task.title==record[\\\"title\\\"]; assert task.dependencies==record[\\\"dependencies\\\"]; assert task.source_specifications==record[\\\"source_specifications\\\"]; assert task.source_catalogue_ids==record[\\\"source_catalogue_ids\\\"]; assert task.authoring_batch==record[\\\"authoring_batch\\\"]; assert task.factory_stages==record[\\\"factory_stages\\\"]; assert task.asset_impact==record[\\\"asset_impact\\\"] and task.asset_ids==record[\\\"asset_ids\\\"]; assert len(task.acceptance_criteria)==3; print(\\\"loader-and-manifest comparison: PASS\\\")' && rg -n '\"'^## (Objective|Dependencies|Ownership|Required behaviour|Web and PWA differences|Non-goals|Asset assessment|Verification|Evidence|Acceptance criteria)$'\"' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md | wc -l && test \\\"\"'$(rg -l '\"'\"'^task_id: R0012$'\"' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks -g 'R*.md' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\\\" = 1 && echo 'unique R0012 ID: PASS' && git diff --check -- projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..682eca0b41aab322e6bfcecdbe577a6f46d2f32f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,152 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0012\n+sequence: 12\n+title: Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\n+dependencies: R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008\n+requirement_ids: NFR-0012,NFR-0010,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability,specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0012\n+authoring_batch: B0006\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: n